<p>Sometimes I just want a nice, easy, CMS for blogging. Emacs and a few lisp function are not that, so I asked Claude Code to make me a web app.</p>
<p>At 7:00 am I sent the following to Claude:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>My blog at baty.net is managed locally using Eleventy. I would like to build a local web app that allows me to create new content. It should have  &quot;New Post&quot;, &quot;New Journal&quot;, &quot;New Page&quot;, and &quot;New Note&quot; options. The editor should handle Markdown, but it doesn't necessarily have to be &quot;WYSIWYG&quot; . There's should be a way to start the local server (&quot;just serve&quot;) and deploy (&quot;just deploy&quot;). The blog is currently in ~/sites/baty.net.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I walked away and made breakfast.</p>
